# Lada Riva 2105/2107 four-door saloon, 1979-2012.
#
# The Riva, a re-engineered Fiat 124: 4,145 mm long, 1,620 mm wide, 1,446 mm
# high, 2,424 mm wheelbase; 1.2-1.7 petrol, rear-wheel drive, live rear axle.
# Britain's cheapest new car through the 1980s and a common 1980s-90s sight;
# UK sales ended in 1997, Russian production in 2012.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lada_Riva
#
# Colours: White, Red, Blue and Green are documented Lada colours of the period.
#
# Weight: 90 in total (white 30, red 25, blue 20, green 15).
#
# Speed 140 km/h; comfort 50/405 (line). Classes 0,1,2.
# Dates: 1979-2012 with a road tail to about 2016.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/lada-riva.blend. References:
# citycars/references/lada-riva/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

